{"id":"word:hebrew:H5331","type":"word","title":"נֶצַח","subtitle":"H5331 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, a goal , i.e. the bright object at a distance travelled towards; hence (figuratively), splendor , or (subjectively) truthfulness , or (objectively) confidence ; but usually (adverbially), continually (i.e. to the most distant point of view)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נֶצַח (H5331) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 43 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נֶצַח (netsach) means properly, a goal , i.e. the bright object at a distance travelled towards; hence (figuratively), splendor , or (subjectively) truthfulness , or (objectively) confidence ; but usually (adverbially), continually (i.e. to the most distant point of view) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 29 11."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נֶצַח","transliteration":"netsach","pronunciation":"neh'-tsakh","strong":"H5331","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5331","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["לָ/נֶ֑צַח","לָ/נֶֽצַח","לָ/נֶ֖צַח","לָ/נֶ֔צַח","לָ/נֶ֥צַח"],"morphs":[["HR/Ncmsa",30],["HNcmsa",7],["HC/Td/Ncmsa",1],["HNcmsc",1],["HTi/R/Ncmsa",1],["HR/Ncmsc",1],["HNcmpa",1],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, a goal , i.e. the bright object at a distance travelled towards; hence (figuratively), splendor , or (subjectively) truthfulness , or (objectively) confidence ; but usually (adverbially), continually (i.e. to the most distant point of view)","usage":"alway(-s), constantly, end, ( n-) ever(more), perpetual, strength, victory.","full":"H5331. netsach I. נֵ֫צַח noun masculine Lam 3:18 eminence, enduring, everlastingness, perpetuity ( לנצח Ecclus 40:14 as 4 below); — נֵ֫צַח 1Sam 15:29 3 t.; נֶ֫צַח Amos 1:11 36t.; suffix נִצְחִי Lam 3:18 ; plural נְצָחִים 34:10; — 1 eminence: ישׂראל נצח the Eminence of Israel ( ׳י ) 1Sam 15:29 (Dr Sam. 98 glory of Israel ); attribute of God 1Chr 29:11 (|| תפארת הוד, et al.). 2 enduring of life , and so life itself as enduring: נִצְחִי אָבַד Lam 3:18 my endurance doth vanish (De sap of life, see II. ׳נ ). 3 endurance in time: נ ׳משׁאות Psa 74:3 perpetual desolations ; ׳לנ יְדַבֵּר Prov 21:28 speaketh continually (?; see Toy); ׳עדנֿ Psa 49:20 unto the end (a long duration), so Job 34:36 . 4 everlastingness, ever , usually לָנֶצַח for ever , 2Sam 2:26 ; Isa 13:20 ; 25:8 ; 28:28 ; 33:20 ; 57:16 ; Jer 3:5 ; 50:39 ; Amos 8:7 ; Hab 1:4 ; Psa 9:7 ; 9:19 ; 10:11 ; 44:24 ; 49:10 ; 52:7 ; 68:17 ; 74:1 ; 74:10 ; 74:19 ; 77:9 ; 79:5 ; 89:47 ; 103:9 ; Job 4:20 ; 14:20 ; 20:7 ; 23:7 ; 36:7 ; Lam 5:20 ; נצחים לנצח (compare עולמים עולם ) Isa 34:10 ; seldom abbreviated נֶצַח Amos 1:11 ( ᵐ5 ׳לָנ We Now GASm), Jer 15:18 ; Psa 13:2 ; 16:11 . II. נצח (√ of following; compare Arabic , Lane 2806, 2807 sprinkle ; Ba ES 52 compare Ethiopic spargere, aspergere Di 677 (rare)).","rootNote":"or נֵצַח ; from 5329 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 29 11","keyReferences":["1Chr 29 11","1Sam 15 29","2Sam 2 26","Amos 1 11","Amos 8 7","Hab 1 4","Isa 13 20","Isa 25 8"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":43,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 29 11","book":"1Chr","chapter":29,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הַ/נֵּ֣צַח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Td/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 15 29","book":"1Sam","chapter":15,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נֵ֣צַח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"2Sam 2 26","book":"2Sam","chapter":2,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הֲ/לָ/נֶ֨צַח֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi/R/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Amos 1 11","book":"Amos","chapter":1,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נֶֽצַח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"Amos 8 7","book":"Amos","chapter":8,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לָ/נֶ֖צַח","sourc